Answer that encryption is available in the browser. This has no effect.

It was meant to let stored secrets survive a restart, and it never did.
BrowserSecretStorageService passes useInMemoryStorage=true to
BaseSecretStorageService, which asks isEncryptionAvailable() only when that flag
is false, so the answer below is never read. Measured on a device: a secret an
extension stored was gone once the app was swiped from recents and reopened.

What keeps secrets is the workbench's own LocalStorageSecretStorageProvider,
switched on at runtime by the vscode-secret-key-path cookie the app sets, with
its key answered by VSCodroidWebViewClient (see SecretStorageKey).

Kept only because removing it, or correcting the comment inside the hunk, changes
the patch set and so needs the server rebuilt. Drop it with the next rebuild.

